# The DIM=32 ASYMMETRIC MX tests (32x32 mesh): different-format activation x weight, BF16 output. These live
# in the bareMetalC ISA suite; simq resolves the names against build_mx_rocket/bareMetalC/<name>-baremetal.
#
#   sim/simq run CONFIG=MxDim32AllAsymGemminiRocketConfig BINARY=baremetal/mxgemmini/asym_dim32.jobs JOBS=8
#
# IMPORTANT: run under CONFIG=MxDim32AllAsymGemminiRocketConfig (dim32 + ALL 12 PE modes, sym+asym), NOT the
# DIM=16 configs. Build the ELFs first: ../../software/gemmini-rocc-tests/build_mx_rocket.sh bareMetalC
# Spike cross-check (all PASS as of 2026-09-21): spike --extension=gemmini_dim32 build_spike/bareMetalC/<name>-baremetal
# Goldens: gen_asym.py (unified, DIM-aware, Spike-consistent). RTL fix: QuantLut.scala DIM-general deproject.
#

